From b763fe0265ecf6b7fe9d3de9b661fb0a7bfd628d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frostbite1536 <125112776+Frostbite1536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:27:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] CUDA: FA vector kernel, pack the Q heads of a K/V head
 for single-token decode with quantized K

With GQA the vector kernel ran one block per Q head, so each K/V head was read and
dequantized once per Q head. For quantized K at one token and GQA >= 3, put 2 or 4 Q
heads into one block (padded heads masked, including their sinks), with the MMA kernel's
(sequence, K/V head, head group) grid mapping; for one head per block the indexing is
unchanged. 4 heads per block for GQA ratios that are a multiple of 4 and for 7, otherwise 2
(V100: 8 heads per block were never faster than 4; GQA 2 stays unpacked).

Q is kept as q8_1 for quantized K, so the extra columns fit: on sm_70 the packed kernels
use 76-163 registers with no spills or local memory, with their key loops unrolled 4x
instead of fully, and the sink loop's columns indexed at compile time (which also removes
most local memory from the existing 2-token kernels). The KQ buffer is sized for the
softmax values too (ncols x nthreads), which 8 columns at D=64 exceeded.
Tests: D 64/128/256, q8_0/q4_0, GQA 3/5/7/12, sinks, 2 sequences, ALiBi.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec.cuh | 115 +++++++++++++++++++++----------
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp       |  13 ++++
 2 files changed, 91 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

